{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen","id":374645,"title":"What's the difference between Kuei-Jin and Risen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-18T18:27:42-08:00","id":374645,"title":"What's the difference between Kuei-Jin and Risen?","content":"<i>Kindred of the East</i> gets a lot of hate, but it does have some strong-standing fans. While many argue for the complete removal of Kuei-Jin in favor of Asian Kindred/Cainites, I have to wonder why the Kuei-Jin are distinguished from Risen (from WtO) in any regard.<br /> <br /> They struggle between the Hun and P'o is already a part of Wraith, existing as the analogues for the Psyche and Shadow in the Dark Kingdom of Jade. Similarly, especially driven wraiths can pull the necessary strings and find the necessary power to re-inhabit their old bodies. With regret or sin being the primary motivator for most Kuei-Jin rebirths, those could easily be described as Passions that motivated the attempt to become Risen. Add in the fact that the 1,000 Hells and their Yama Kings exist as an established part of Dark Kingdom of Jade lore and you're left with Kuei-Jin in all but name, missing only a <i>chi</i> system, some of their powers, and the heavy focus on the Xue myth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 01-18-2015, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T19:37:24-08:00","id":374687,"title":"","content":"The biggest difference is that the Keui-jin happen to have dharmas to follow to find a path to salvation. Their ties to the yin and yang Chi is also unique as it enables them to have certain curses broken or at last retarded enough to allow them to act. There is also a larger population of kuei-jin than Risen. Risen need the help of a Guild and keui-jin can arise independantly. <br /> Are there similarities? Of course. Anyone would be foolish to deny that. But are there also differences? Yes. What I have stated thus far is the product of a mind addled by lack of sleep and so others can expound on the further differences far better than what I can. I am giving only the ones that spring to mind on first thoughts of the stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T19:38:09-08:00","id":374688,"title":"","content":"In Risen the hun and po stay together. In an urn, they split at the moment of death, and the vigor soul (po) goes to hell for an indeterminate amount of time (extremely traditional characters might go in for 49 days, one week for each po division) and then might escape, whereupon it then reunites with its cloud soul and body, even reforming it from cremated ashes. And the newly returned in question is usually a chi mei, or flesh-eater, without any faculties and possessed of the desire to do exactly what their name suggests until they can be captured and brought to heel.<br /> <br /> In contrast, Risen just cut a deal with their Shadow, or Po in this case, and they get to stay in the skinlands as long as their anchor and purpose remain intact. They're generally a lot closer to finding any good way out of their existence than one of the Demon People.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:13:30-08:00","id":374756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I have to wonder why the Kuei-Jin are distinguished from Risen (from WtO) in any regard. </div> </div> </div>Read the books and you should notice there are considerable differences.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They struggle between the Hun and P'o is already a part of Wraith, existing as the analogues for the Psyche and Shadow in the Dark Kingdom of Jade. </div> </div> </div>True though the struggle has a different meaning and unlike in Wraith the Po usually shares the Psyches willingness to avoid self-destructive actions, the Po knows the consequences waiting for it and is here precisely because it wanted to avoid them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With regret or sin being the primary motivator for most Kuei-Jin rebirths </div> </div> </div>While the Psyche might be motivated by regret it has little bearing on their Rebirth, the Kuei-Jin take their second breath only if they possess strong and cunning enough Po to escape Hell. Po's motivations for this usually being only to avoid the eternal suffering offered by the Hell's not a regret for it's actions. Another component needed is exceptionally strong willed Psyche or else they risk becoming a Yulan-Jin or being unable to take the second breath at all.<br /> Rising on the other hand requires that the Wraith learn certain Arcanoi, usually needing a teacher, making a deal with their Shadow to get the permission to Rise and they remain dead things driven by the emotions that prevented them from moving on, Kuei-Jin are here because their souls were ripped apart and their Po's prevented from moving on by being condemned to eternal suffering while the Psyche was condemned to remain with the corpse becoming undeath upon the escape of the Po regardless of what the Psyche wants as long as it has had the will to remain till the Po returns. With Risen both halves of the soul must agree upon the concept of rising or it doesn't work. Also Risen need a conduit to hold their Shadows while they return while the Kuei-Jin share the same corporeal form being bound to it in a way risen are not, any risen can leave it's body behind and return to being a Wraith and the other way around.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Add in the fact that the 1,000 Hells and their Yama Kings exist as an established part of Dark Kingdom of Jade lore </div> </div> </div>1k Hells share a single path that reaches from the Yin world to the Yomi worlds and that is pretty much it but the same is true of the Yomi and Yang world. And yes they do have a established part in each others lore but same is true of pretty much all lines. WtA has Vampires called Setites does this mean that Werewolves are very similar to the Vampires, no only that they share a world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> missing only a <i>chi</i> system </div> </div> </div>Kuei-Jin are defined by their hunger for Chi so this is fairly major difference equal to the difference between Risens Pathos pool and a Vampires Bloodpool. That is both empower the creature they belong to but come from very different sources and mean very different things. Chi has more in common with Bloodpool that it does Pathos. Chi system also broadly defines the Kuei-Jins susceptibility to the Fire and Wave souls, Frenzy and R\u00f6tschreck respectively, both of which the Risen lack, as well as defining how close to life/death the Kuei-Jin are bodily amongst other things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> some of their powers </div> </div> </div>Try all of their powers, Risen share 4 western Disciplines with the Kindred and have access to Arcanoi both which are lacking in the Kuei-Jin who have their own powersets. The difference is again comparing Gifts and Arts/Realms or werewolves and Changelings for example. They share about the same amount of things between themselves.<br /> <br /> Also you forget Dharmas and the Enlightenment sought by the Kuei-Jin, and used by them to reign in their Po's, unless that with all it's mechanical weights, also completely lacking in Risen, is meant to be included in the Xue myth despite half of the Dharmas having nothing to do with Xue.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of other differences like effects of Sunlight and many many others but unfortunately I have not the time now as I'm already late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:37:25-08:00","id":374810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen#post374645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Kindred of the East</i> gets a lot of hate, but it does have some strong-standing fans. While many argue for the complete removal of Kuei-Jin in favor of Asian Kindred/Cainites, I have to wonder why the Kuei-Jin are distinguished from Risen (from WtO) in any regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>because they aren't Risen. Wow that was easy. KOTE takes liberally from Vampire, Werewolf, Mage and Wraith to make a game that is much more the &quot;vampire that exists as part of a meta world of darkness&quot; than &quot;ok here's this stuff about the bible!&quot; Hun and Po are no where near as central as Dharma. Some Dharmas even support nuturing PO(this is mechanically questionable but there's a reason why I think KOTE needs a serious clean up)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T20:44:26-08:00","id":374817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=374756#post374756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1k Hells share a single path that reaches from the Yin world to the Yomi worlds and that is pretty much it but the same is true of the Yomi and Yang world. And yes they do have a established part in each others lore but same is true of pretty much all lines. WtA has Vampires called Setites does this mean that Werewolves are very similar to the Vampires, no only that they share a world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Names. They share names. They're no more required to share a world than St. Elsewhere is with any of the TV shows that it could technically crossover with (<a href=\"http://www.slushfactory.com/content/EpupypyZAZTDOLwdfz.php\" target=\"_blank\">the list, as cited by the late Dwayne McDuffie, is considerable</a>).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T22:52:21-08:00","id":374897,"title":"","content":"Even the writers noticed the similarity - I believe at one point in the corebook, they even referred to kuei-jin as &quot;spectres that have found a way to Rise&quot;. In feel, though, there are strong differences in tone (and some mechanics)<br /> <br /> Strip away the trappings of the game, and a Risen occurs when a ghost finds a way to reanimate its corpse as a zombie, and then possesses said zombie. As such, it has many of the best traits of both types of undead. It has a physical body, but feels no pain. It retains most of the wraith's arcanoi, and can continue to learn more. And since there <i>is</i> &quot;someone home&quot;, the Risen isn't some shambling mess - in fact, it can even learn celerity (super speed) like a vampire.<br /> <br /> A Risen, though, is also very, <i>very</i> dead. And any doctor would almost immediately notice that. The Risen's body is cold to the touch (room temp, in fact), has no heart beat, no pulse . . . Most Risen even have embalming fluid, not blood, in their veins.<br /> <br /> A kuei-jin, on the other hand, was never a wraith. They start out as damned souls, often ones that the Yama Kings are trying to turn into demons (<i>a la </i>Spawn). They manage to escape (or are released) from their hell, and escape back to the living world . . .<br /> <br /> The result is a being that while <i>sort of</i> alive (some kuei-jin can even have kids), has no way to refuel their energy reserves &quot;naturally&quot;. While they can eat food, they gain no nourishment. They have no fetters, and no passions (at least not like a wraith). The only way a kuei-jin can maintain her chi base, is by ripping chi from the flesh/blood/souls of the living - which kind of makes sense, given their proto-demon status.<br /> <br /> If it helps, think of it this way. A kuei-jin 's soul <i>has </i>been judged, and sent to an afterlife in hell. A wraith (and thus a Risen) is a soul that has not, and refuses to be, judged until its unfinished business is completed. Thus, when they get their bodies back, there are substantial differences in how that body functions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i><u>Edit</u></i>: Also, a Risen technically has <i>two</i> bodies. Unlike a kuei-jin, a Risen's shadow &quot;lives&quot; in the Conduit (often a former fetter), while the Psyche resides in the zombie-body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4624,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","user":"One Vorlon","date":". 01-19-2015, 05:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-18T23:43:56-08:00","id":374942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=374897#post374897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it helps, think of it this way. A kuei-jin 's soul <i>has </i>been judged, and sent to an afterlife in hell. A wraith (and thus a Risen) is a soul that has not, and refuses to be, judged until its unfinished business is completed. Thus, when they get their bodies back, there are substantial differences in how that body functions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't mean for this to be a tangent, but given this logic, is it possible that a wraith (or possible risen) &quot;passes on&quot; and comes back as a kuei-jin later in existence?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T02:26:21-08:00","id":375032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=374942#post374942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mean for this to be a tangent, but given this logic, is it possible that a wraith (or possible risen) &quot;passes on&quot; and comes back as a kuei-jin later in existence?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm . . . Good question. As far as I know, there are no rules for that situation. It would have to be an Asian wraith/Risen . . . hmm . . . You've got the strong Psyche/hun, the potent (and awake) Shadow/P'o to rip apart the Shroud . . . If one of the Yama Kings grabbed a &quot;dying&quot; wraith before Oblivion could devour them . . . hmm . . .maybe. Off-hand, I don't know of anything in the rules that would prevent it. Such a being would be a one-in-a-billion entity, but, yeah - why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T03:40:16-08:00","id":375117,"title":"","content":"So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T05:27:38-08:00","id":375174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375117#post375117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't go there. There be monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T07:47:28-08:00","id":375254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375117#post375117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>Something having to do with Wraith and paradigms of death, presumably. Wait until Wr20 comes out, or go glut yourself on Wraith books until you find something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T14:30:00-08:00","id":375582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375117#post375117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>There be monsters? Come now, surely none of us would suggest it is because 'durr hurr Asian souls are different because racism.' For want of a better term, 'paradigms of death' is the most logical reason. Why are there different Dark Kingdoms at all? Because the expectations and legends of the Quick shape the Underworld. The beliefs, mythology and worldview of countless generations of the folks living in Asia has changed how their dead act on a metaphysical level...<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:12:05-08:00","id":375736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375117#post375117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Why Do Kitsune only happen in Asia when Red Foxes are one of the most common species on on the planet? Why did Ancient Egyptians have 5 aspected Souls?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:18:19-08:00","id":375742,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=Lian;n375736] Why Do Kitsune only happen in Asia when Red Foxes are one of the most common species on on the planet? QUOTE]<br /> Bai Mianxi awaked in Asia and it was relatively recently. I do actually assume that there are Kitsune spreading slowly across the world. There is little reason they shouldn't be. Having one parent died as a result of the child also slows their expansion significantly though.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375736#post375736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why did Ancient Egyptians have 5 aspected Souls?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'm not as familiar with the new mummy books, so I don't have an answer for this one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:35:29-08:00","id":375750,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=idpersona;n375742]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375736#post375736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why Do Kitsune only happen in Asia when Red Foxes are one of the most common species on on the planet? QUOTE]<br /> Bai Mianxi awaked in Asia and it was relatively recently. I do actually assume that there are Kitsune spreading slowly across the world. There is little reason they shouldn't be. Having one parent died as a result of the child also slows their expansion significantly though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not as familiar with the new mummy books, so I don't have an answer for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was throwing out &quot;just like in the real world there are animals enviorments that aren't universal the same is true of the Supernatural&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T18:46:18-08:00","id":375755,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=idpersona;n375742]<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375736#post375736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Why Do Kitsune only happen in Asia when Red Foxes are one of the most common species on on the planet? QUOTE]<br /> Bai Mianxi awaked in Asia and it was relatively recently. I do actually assume that there are Kitsune spreading slowly across the world. There is little reason they shouldn't be. Having one parent died as a result of the child also slows their expansion significantly though.<br /> I'm not as familiar with the new mummy books, so I don't have an answer for this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Funny tangent. In NWoD other sources mention a five part soul. Mage actually discussed it first to the best of my knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T03:13:46-08:00","id":377078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen#post374645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Kindred of the East</i> gets a lot of hate, but it does have some strong-standing fans. While many argue for the complete removal of Kuei-Jin in favor of Asian Kindred/Cainites, I have to wonder why the Kuei-Jin are distinguished from Risen (from WtO) in any regard.<br /> <br /> They struggle between the Hun and P'o is already a part of Wraith, existing as the analogues for the Psyche and Shadow in the Dark Kingdom of Jade. Similarly, especially driven wraiths can pull the necessary strings and find the necessary power to re-inhabit their old bodies. With regret or sin being the primary motivator for most Kuei-Jin rebirths, those could easily be described as Passions that motivated the attempt to become Risen. Add in the fact that the 1,000 Hells and their Yama Kings exist as an established part of Dark Kingdom of Jade lore and you're left with Kuei-Jin in all but name, missing only a <i>chi</i> system, some of their powers, and the heavy focus on the Xue myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I see it, the basilar state of a Risen is a Wraith, an immaterial soul, she is a Risen only for a short term (and often is not a healty stay).<br /> On the other hand a Kuei-Jin basilar state is a walking and not-certainly-rotting corpse, he can leave said body for a short term, but as long as he (un)live he will return.<br /> Basically they are two splats that deal with the same concepts, but taking it on from opposite sides.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T23:37:05-08:00","id":380816,"title":"","content":"I meant to address the thematic differences between Risen and Kuei-Jin on the next day after my last post but had no time before going away for a week so here I am now. And there seems to be more questions and such that have risen up on the subject.<br /> <br /> Thematically there is a huge gap between the two supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Risen Thematics involve things left undone and emotions strong enough to not only win over death itself but also to drive the Wraith that is born from it all to break all laws of his kind to break through the wall between the living and the dead to Rise for a specific purpose, this purpose is it's Passions. So in other words playing a Risen is about playing a very obsessed person willing to do anything to reach the goals of his obsession. They are driven by raw emotion honed to razor sharpness by the details of his Passion.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin thematic involve the search for enlightenment along with the struggle to balance it with your new nature as a parasitic entity that is prone to be overwhelmed by raw instincts of flight and fight and all this against a backdrop of having escaped a very literal Hell and with full knowledge that loosing the narrow path that leads to enlightenment will likely cast you back to that very Hell. There is no emotion driven clarity of purpose. There is no conscious decision to rise into undeath which is actually only a consequence of the Po succeeding in the seemingly impossible, but very understandable, attempt to escape his eternal torment. The Po has no plan of what he wants to do once he escapes only that it wants to escape it's torments and tormentors. When a Kuei-Jin first draws his second breath he is little more than an animal driven by instinct, unlike Risen who are very aware of themselves having made conscious decision to rise and having had to work to learn the method to do so, until they are found by other or some other circumstance snaps them to consciousness after which they need to find a way to hang on to something that will help them keep their minds and souls intact. That is the Dharma, a way towards not only enlightenment but power as well. Dharma leads to power, enlightenment and a sort of Transcendence while a Risen striving towards Transcendence, not a goal most Risen have usually Transcendence would be easier for a Wraith to find in it's normal state, will actually weaken itself during that search losing Passions which act as their power source.<br /> <br /> Mechanics work pretty well to enforce these themes as well. Where a Risen reaching towards it's goal, acting in accordance to it's Passions, will be empowered by that act alone and only working to strengthen their resolve towards their goals Kuei-Jin are constantly distracted from their goals by their need to feed, their parasitic nature dominating them utterly in the end, along with the optional distraction of undead politics, a possible distraction for a Risen as well though only likely succumbed to if it allows them to indulge their Passions.<br /> <br /> So again where Risen are driven towards a certain goal them striving towards that goal acts to empower them, filling their Pathos reserves, where as Kuei-Jin striving towards his goals usually bleeds Chi through their efforts and must turn away from whatever they were striving towards to feed and regain their strength.<br /> <br /> The most fundamental difference is that Risen are self-empowering and Kuei-Jin are parasitic predators and that difference alone does much to drive their themes apart. Also Kuei-Jin are divided between balancing both his Yin and Yang as well as his Hun and Po where as the Risen only balances between his Psyche and Shadow.<br /> <br /> As another minor mechanical difference Risen need their own bodies to rise, where as some Kuei-Jin draw their second breath in a body not their own and Yulan-Jin jump between bodies throughout their existence, and those bodies must have an intact brain and heart while Kuei-Jin occasionally form their bodies even from ash at the time of their return having no such requirements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> spectres that have found a way to Rise </div> </div> </div>These are possible through normal means of rising but they are still extremely rare as the Shadow, dominant though it may be, still needs the approval of his Psyche to Rise even in the case of a Spectre just like a normal Risen must have the approval of his Shadow to actually Rise. They are mechanically and thematically no different from a normal Risen though they would likely have a somewhat darker themes than even the normal Risen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia? </div> </div> </div>Officially it's because of the Paradigms of death that govern souls belonging to the Dark Kingdom of Jade's jurisdiction. Basically it is the same reason why souls of Dark Kingdom of Jade origin loose their access to their unique Arcanoi, the Ways, if they are left stranded for prolonged times outside their Dark Kingdom, see Wraith the Great War for details about that.<br /> <br /> Still one could also argue, and make a slight retcon to correct this issue into less of an racial issue, that it is becouse those lands are the ones under the influence of the Yama Kings and that the possibility of Kuei-Jin happening elsewhere is only a matter of time as Yomi lengthens it's area of influence outwards, as it has in some cases at places where the Kanbutsian(sp? not near my books) draw their second breaths.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why Do Kitsune only happen in Asia when Red Foxes are one of the most common species on on the planet? </div> </div> </div>Presumably the explanation for this is that they are a young species having been created only after the Wars of Rage and thus they have not had the time to spread outside the lands they were born in. That is to say should a Kitsune start breeding with red foxes in Europe it would be likely that new Kitsune would start to be born there at some point. So it's not about how spread out the Red Fox is but how has the spiritual factor that makes Kitsune possible spread since their creation in Asia. Just like a wolves with no Garou blood at all, no Kinfolk etc, would not just spontaneously give birth to a Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T08:18:23-08:00","id":381021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Possessed</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=380816#post380816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Kanbutsian(sp? not near my books) draw their second breaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kanbujian. Kan means to look, Bu is a negative modifier or simply no or not, jian means to see. Hence, &quot;blind&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T03:36:54-08:00","id":391209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/374645-what-s-the-difference-between-kuei-jin-and-risen?p=375117#post375117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So on that note. Why is it that kuei-jin only happen in Asia?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually a question being researched in-game by several groups, including the Giovanni and the Heaven Suffusing Surgeons (a group of kuei-jin participating in the Great Leap Outwards - i.e. the invasion of California). Paradigms of death seem to be a big factor - and not just on a societal level. The &quot;urn&quot; (future kuei-jin) apparently has to believe that its possible - that they could go to Yomi/hell, escape, and come back as one of the Hungry Dead.<br /> <br /> Another key aspect seems to be the presence of other kuei-jin. There were plenty of true believers in various Chinatown (and other Asian immigrant communities) throughout California, for generatoins - but the first recorded case of a North American kuei-jin didn't happen until <i>after</i> the kuei-jin invaded California<br /> <br /> And you also seem to need a Yama King to torture the future kuei-jin's soul - for some reason, Western demon lords don't count. But there also seems to be an X-factor, too. One that no one can account for . . . yet","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}